  "body": "From: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#dom-input-value-value\r\n\r\n> 5. If the element's value (after applying the value sanitization algorithm) is different from oldValue, and the element has a text entry cursor position, move the text entry cursor position to the end of the text control, unselecting any selected text and resetting the selection direction to \"none\".\r\n\r\nThis seems like it only deals with appending text to a value.\r\n\r\nWhat should the cursor position be at the end of the following:\r\n\r\n1. Imagine an input with a state:\r\n\r\n        value=\"Brek\"\r\n        selectionStart=3\r\n        selectionEnd=3\r\n\r\n1. Apply the new value: \"Break\" (in this case, a user typed \"a\")\r\n1. Expected end state:\r\n\r\n        value=\"Break\"\r\n        selectionStart=4\r\n        selectionEnd=4\r\n\r\n1. Actual end state:\r\n\r\n        value=\"Break\"\r\n        selectionStart=5\r\n        selectionEnd=5",
